[{:db/id -1, :doc/id "doc-ayatori-bench-coscientist-iteration-40", :doc/title "ayatori Co-Scientist Iteration 40 — the served/in-process gap was pacing onto efficiency cores, not the engine", :doc/path "bench/coscientist-iteration-40.edn", :doc/body "# Co-Scientist iteration 40 - the served/in-process gap was the pacing, not the engine\n\n> Seed: iteration 39's S31. Judge: bench/benchmark.edn v2; rung :sf1-full;\n> SUT levi, driver judah, LAN.\n\n## Generate / Rank\n\n  Served IC09 was ~12 ms p50 while the same code in one process measured\n  4.9 ms on the same parameters. Ruled out in order: the parameter files\n  (identical md5 on both hosts); concurrency (1 slot and 8 slots both\n  12.0 ms); the request itself (curl over all 99 parameters back-to-back\n  from levi: p50 4.3 ms; a new `:repeat n` route answers one request n\n  times in a thread: 4.2 ms steady, 4.7-7 on the first call).\n\n  What remained was the driver's PACING. At 32/s with one slot it leaves\n  ~27 ms idle between requests and reads 12.0 ms; the same driver at\n  200/s with one slot -- back-to-back, saturated -- reads 4.8. levi is an\n  Apple M4: 4 performance + 6 efficiency cores. A lightly loaded process\n  is scheduled onto the efficiency cores, about 2.5x slower on this\n  pointer-chasing work, and its caches go cold between requests.\n\n## Reflect\n\n  - No engine change; the finding changes how every server-ms p50 in\n    the receipts since iteration 34 should be read: at low rates it\n    measures efficiency-core placement, at saturation it measures the\n    engine. Ceilings are unaffected -- at the ceiling every core is busy.\n  - M4 restated: the SUT's compute at saturation is ~4 P + 6 E cores,\n    not 10 equal ones; the audited No.1 ran 160 server cores. The\n    hardware ratio is ~30x before any engine difference.\n  - The cheap tool was the decisive one again: one route that repeats a\n    request in-process split 'per-request overhead' from 'steady cost'\n    without a second JVM.\n\n## Meta\n\nVerdict under bench/benchmark.edn v2: no row moved (4374.1 stands); a\nmeasurement rule gained. Ratio to the audited No.1: 32.\n\nSeeds for iteration 41, in order:\n\n  - S32: the binding-set machinery (hasheq of binding maps on every\n    `into #{}`; vectors as bindings inside the drive).\n  - M4: performance cores for the SUT -- a host with more of them.\n  - S26: full-data parameters. S23b: IC05. M3: SF3.\n"}]
